Package: blip
Version: @VERSION@
Section: interpreters
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: metif12 <metif12@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/metif12/blip
Description: a Lisp dialect with real tail calls
 blip is a Lisp dialect implemented in V, with real tail calls,
 pattern matching, and errors as values. This package ships the
 interpreter plus its standard library; run `blip run prog.blip`,
 check `blip test`, or start the REPL with a bare `blip`.
